.TH KEYLIX-VERIFIER 1
.SH NAME
keylix-verifier \- bounded local Keylix sender-binding verifier
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keylix-verifier
.B --socket
.I PATH
.B --peer-credentials
.I PATH
.B --replay-dir
.I PATH
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
keylix-verifier verifies DPoP sender binding for host-validated access credentials.
It does not validate application credentials, construct principals, or authorize
application actions.
.PP
The reference transport is one-request-per-connection JSON over a local Unix
socket. Inner host attestations are decoded only after HMAC authentication of an
allowlisted service peer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " PATH"
Absolute Unix-domain socket path. By default its parent must be a private
service-owned directory reached only through root- or verifier-owned non-writable
path components. A stale owner-matching socket is recovered only when no live
listener accepts a connection.
.TP
.BI --socket-group-gid " GID"
On Linux, permit one explicit trusted local transport group. GID must be
nonzero and the verifier process must have it as its filesystem GID or a
supplementary group. The socket parent must already carry this GID through
setgid and group-traversal-only (02710), with no setuid/sticky bits or POSIX
access/default ACLs. The verifier process must start with umask 0117 so the
socket is created mode 0660 at bind time. The verifier never changes the
directory SGID/publication mode at runtime; the supervisor owns that setup.
This keeps the profile compatible with systemd DynamicUser/RestrictSUIDSGID
sandboxes. Replay state and peer credentials remain owner-only; HMAC peer
authentication remains mandatory.
.TP
.BI --peer-credentials " PATH"
Absolute owner-only JSON peer credential file. The file must be owned by root
or the verifier UID. Each path component is opened descriptor-relative and must
be root- or verifier-owned, non-symlinked, and not group/other-writable.
.TP
.BI --replay-dir " PATH"
Absolute private service-owned persistent replay directory. Replay state
survives verifier restarts. The directory is opened as a capability and replay
operations stay descriptor-relative; untrusted owners, symlinks, and
group/other-writable path components are rejected.
.TP
.BI --require-nonce-context " ID"
Enable sticky server-owned resource-server nonce enforcement for the configured
context.
.TP
.BI --replay-capacity " N"
Maximum active persistent replay entries. Default 4096.
.TP
.BI --nonce-capacity " N"
Maximum process-local nonce contexts. Default 64.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print version.
.SH SECURITY
Replay state is durable across verifier restarts in one owner-only local directory.
Each request and response frame has an absolute two-second I/O deadline.
Multi-instance deployment requires a shared atomic backend or equivalent routing
semantics.
Peer secrets and request credentials must not be placed in source control, Nix
store paths, logs, or command-line arguments.
